WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.720
France deploys 70,000 officers as hundreds of thousands prepared to protest living costs and school conditions this weekend. This is Omni View, episode 215. North Korea's leader reaches a Chinese border city. Washington asks Cubans to work with American intelligence and Iranian plots against Americans are described as advanced, before understanding the issue. President Emmanuel Macron met high school student representatives on Friday, and his advisors said the government would announce commitments

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.400
on school staffing and conditions starting Monday.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.660
The French Interior Ministry has limited authorized marches on Saturday

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.060
to those organized by recognized unions,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.860
and it has banned gatherings in Lyon, Nice, and Montpellier.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.640
Students, trade union members, and other groups are preparing demonstrations in Paris and other cities,

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.040
with police officers and soldiers to be deployed nationwide.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.020
The protests began with high school demands to fix staff shortages

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.060
before violence last weekend.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:03.560
Hundreds of people have already been jailed for vandalism, arson, and looting after fast-track

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.200
court hearings.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:09.660
Interior Minister Laurent Nunez said the ministry will be uncompromising with vandals,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.060
looters, and people committing acts of violence, and he cited calls for violence on social media

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.540
from the far left and the radical extreme left.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.380
Disillusionment remains high over warnings of future deep spending cuts by any incoming government.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.220
What both the security briefings and the organizers describe is the same sequence.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:34.320
School and living cost demands came first, then last weekend's damage, then this weekend's

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.440
tighter rules, where they split is what Saturday is for.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.240
BBC reporting centers on the interior ministry's drive to stop a repeat of looting and arson,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.940
and it carries Nunez's line that vandals will not be spared.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.480
The Guardian instead lingers on community tension after a fatal shooting Friday, West of Paris,

00:01:52.480 --> 00:02:02.520
which the government described as a racist terrorist attack, and it notes that some protests are also planned in Italy, Spain, Austria, Portugal, Albania, and Ireland.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:13.740
Organizers in that same Guardian account say they will keep mobilizing despite the restrictions, and they still present the marches as a push for better school funding and relief from rising living costs.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:20.180
The Guardian also records that Marine Le Pen's national rally is holding its national conference in Orléans,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.080
drawing up to 30,000 counter-demonstrators.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.660
Many Paris metro stations, major museums and tourist sites will close.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:35.060
AP News and France 24 record those museum closures and a 20% increase in policing compared with last weekend.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.860
Even people defending the crackdown are still talking about school staffing promises.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.900
even organizers who reject the Bans are still walking into a weekend defined by them.

00:02:45.776 --> 00:02:51.096
North Korean leader Kim Jong-un crossed into China on the newly open New Yalu River bridge

00:02:51.096 --> 00:02:54.236
and arrived in the border city of Dandong on Saturday.

00:02:55.116 --> 00:03:00.896
Japan Times reporting places the trip one day before the anniversary of Chinese troops entering the Korean War.

00:03:01.436 --> 00:03:07.016
The four-lane bridge was completed in 2014, but it had sat unused until recently

00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:11.436
because connecting roads and customs facilities were missing on the North Korean side.

00:03:12.136 --> 00:03:16.516
The visit comes after North Korea and Russia opened their first road bridge last month.

00:03:17.176 --> 00:03:21.876
China is North Korea's largest trading partner and a main source of diplomatic, economic,

00:03:22.236 --> 00:03:27.476
and political support for the isolated, nuclear-armed state, though the two countries' relations

00:03:27.476 --> 00:03:28.936
have not always been smooth.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:34.556
Deutsche Vela treats the bridge opening as a step toward stronger economic ties, while

00:03:34.556 --> 00:03:39.036
While noting that those ties have varied over time, trade with China in that account

00:03:39.036 --> 00:03:42.696
could supply goods needed to develop North Korea's civilian economy.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:47.376
Both outlets set the Dandong arrival against that recent run of infrastructure.

00:03:47.956 --> 00:03:52.916
The unused Chinese span now opened, and the new road link with Russia already in use.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:58.660
Washington asked Cuban seeking political change to form a discrete partnership with the Central

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.760
Intelligence Agency, or CIA.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:06.280
The United States Secretary of State Marco Rubio put that appeal on social media on Friday,

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.360
framing it as a way to end the communist government.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.920
Al Jazeera reports the post against months of United States pressure on Havana, including

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.560
an oil blockade that has contributed to fuel shortages and blackouts.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.000
United States President Donald Trump and other senior officials have for months openly hinted

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:29.820
at military intervention and a permanent presence in Cuba, ramping up economic, political, and

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:35.020
legal pressure. In Rubio's own framing, people who want change should not wait on speeches.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:41.140
They should work quietly with American intelligence. Cuban Deputy Foreign Minister Carlos Fernandez

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:47.060
DeCosio answered on the same platform, calling the appeal a sign of desperation within the agency.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:52.640
He said there must be a great deal of desperation or misery within the agency for it to be forced to

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.340
sell its services like a tube of toothpaste. United Nations rights experts have condemned the oil

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:03.880
blockade as a violation of international law. Rights advocates say the Trump administration's

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:09.140
threats have echoed an imperialist approach. Al Jazeera's account is an escalation story,

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.120
the blockade, the hints of force, then a public invitation to work with the CIA, followed

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.057
by Havana's rebuttal that the agency is hawking itself. A United States intelligence memo sent

00:05:21.057 --> 00:05:25.817
to Secretary of State Marco Rubio states that Iranian plots to kill Americans have reached

00:05:25.817 --> 00:05:30.837
advanced stages in the Middle East and other countries. The Hindu reports that warning in the

00:05:30.837 --> 00:05:35.837
context of heightened regional tensions, and it ties the memo to Washington's order this week

00:05:35.837 --> 00:05:41.017
for non-essential embassy staff and families to leave Saudi Arabia amid attacks from Yemen's

00:05:41.017 --> 00:05:46.657
Houthis. The memo went after that evacuation order at the United States Embassy in Saudi Arabia.

00:05:47.297 --> 00:05:52.477
Fox News adds that the plots are assessed as having reached advanced stages, and that the locations

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:58.189
named include the Middle East and other countries. Mauritius' state-owned airline is examining

00:05:58.189 --> 00:06:03.689
the addition of single-Isle aircraft as part of a long-term strategy review. The carrier is

00:06:03.689 --> 00:06:08.789
planning to add narrow-body jets while reassessing earlier plans to acquire wide-body planes.

00:06:09.549 --> 00:06:14.909
Bloomberg presents the review as a shift in fleet planning, without timelines or a final decision.

00:06:15.995 --> 00:06:20.895
Foreign institutional investors have sold Indian stocks for a 10th consecutive week as markets

00:06:20.895 --> 00:06:21.955
its continued to slide.

00:06:22.475 --> 00:06:27.175
The Economic Times reports that selling streak and asks whether the worst has passed or

00:06:27.175 --> 00:06:28.695
further declines lie ahead.

00:06:29.508 --> 00:06:32.848
Ukraine reports progress worth knowing on military starlink.

00:06:33.408 --> 00:06:36.308
The connections are working again after speed limits were lifted.

00:06:36.908 --> 00:06:42.248
SpaceX had imposed those limits on October 14th, and they were removed after high-level talks.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:47.148
The restrictions had limited drone operations that rely on the terminals, and the terminals

00:06:47.148 --> 00:06:49.028
had been hampered since mid-October.

00:06:49.028 --> 00:06:53.108
However, Wall Street Journal reporting notes that the restoration improves connectivity

00:06:53.108 --> 00:06:54.648
for Ukrainian forces.

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:59.868
A related community report describes the terminals now operating above 400 kilometers

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:00.488
per hour.

00:07:01.513 --> 00:07:06.413
Across other desks, Bolivian teachers began a nationwide strike, with hundreds demanding

00:07:06.413 --> 00:07:09.153
higher pay and warning against privatization.

00:07:09.693 --> 00:07:14.673
The ruling coalition in Czechia pushed public media funding reforms through an initial parliamentary

00:07:14.673 --> 00:07:16.933
vote despite opposition criticism.

00:07:17.553 --> 00:07:22.393
Residents and analysts in Southern Lebanon see little prospect of policy change after

00:07:22.393 --> 00:07:24.613
the October 27th Israeli vote.

00:07:25.233 --> 00:07:29.953
Forensic teams in Argentina have identified at least 38 victims of the country's last

00:07:29.953 --> 00:07:31.233
military dictatorship.

00:07:32.173 --> 00:07:37.213
Myanmar's detained leader, Aung Sang-Su-Chi, spoke with her son for the first time in five years,

00:07:37.753 --> 00:07:39.473
and the call included health concerns.

00:07:40.499 --> 00:07:45.259
Coverage of a French demonstration day is easy to misread, and to really understand the

00:07:45.259 --> 00:07:49.239
outcome you have to follow the authorization rules, not only the crowd.

00:07:49.879 --> 00:07:54.839
The common mix-up is to treat every march as a single legal object, either allowed or

00:07:54.839 --> 00:07:59.639
forbidden, when the system actually sorts organizers before anyone steps into the street.

00:08:00.219 --> 00:08:04.919
French law requires organizers to declare a demonstration in advance to local authorities.

00:08:05.559 --> 00:08:10.139
Those authorities can impose root changes or conditions rather than a simple yes or no.

00:08:10.139 --> 00:08:16.019
Under recent decrease, only March is backed by recognized trade unions receive automatic protection.

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:20.179
When the Interior Ministry or City officials issue a blanket ban,

00:08:20.819 --> 00:08:24.279
groups without union sponsorship must cancel or risk dispersal.

00:08:24.799 --> 00:08:27.019
That design gives the state wide discretion,

00:08:27.479 --> 00:08:31.099
and it still lets very large events proceed when unions are on the paperwork.

00:08:31.839 --> 00:08:37.479
Opposition parties accuse the government of failing to foresee the scale of unrest on October 17th,

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:42.439
And the same rulebook is why a union stamp and a student meeting can matter more than a slogan.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:47.180
Prefecture orders and union calls to action are the primary papers.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.540
Ministry statements are the plan, not yet the street.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:55.100
Comparing one city with another shows whether a ban is uniform or local.

00:08:56.049 --> 00:08:58.469
When you next read that a French march was restricted,

00:08:58.989 --> 00:09:03.669
check whether the limit applies to every gathering or only to groups without a recognized sponsor.

00:09:03.669 --> 00:09:08.589
BBC dwells on the ministry's violence prevention brief and the extra officers.

00:09:08.989 --> 00:09:14.069
The Guardian dwells on the Friday shooting, the Union and student demands and marches plan

00:09:14.069 --> 00:09:14.869
beyond France.

00:09:15.609 --> 00:09:19.569
The French government is expected to set out those school staffing commitments on Monday.

00:09:20.189 --> 00:09:21.029
That's omnivue.

00:09:21.489 --> 00:09:25.509
The news can feel heavy, but understanding what's actually happening and what's being done

00:09:25.509 --> 00:09:28.009
about it beats doom scrolling every time.

